<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/medina" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/medina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-8">8 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Abdulaziz ibn Saud proclaimed King of the Hejaz</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After conquering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a> was proclaimed King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masjid-al-haram">Great Mosque of Mecca</a>. In 1932 he merged his realms into the Kingdom of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-16">16 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Robert Goddard launches the first liquid-fuelled rocket</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Auburn, Massachusetts, Goddard's petrol and liquid-oxygen rocket flew for 2.5 seconds and rose about 12 metres. The principle underlies most modern space launch vehicles.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-9">9 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Byrd and Bennett claim to fly over the North Pole</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard Byrd and Floyd Bennett flew a Fokker trimotor from Spitsbergen and reported reaching the Pole. Doubts about their speed and navigation have kept the claim in dispute.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-12">12 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Airship Norge crosses the North Pole</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roald-amundsen">Roald Amundsen</a>, Umberto Nobile and Lincoln Ellsworth flew over the Pole in the airship Norge on a flight from Svalbard to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a>. It is the first undisputed arrival at the North Pole.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/may-coup-poland" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/may-coup-poland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/may-coup-poland">May Coup (Poland)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The May Coup was the seizure of power in Poland by Marshal Józef Piłsudski from 12 to 14 May 1926.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/general-strike-of-1926" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/general-strike-of-1926.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/general-strike-of-1926">General Strike of 1926</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The General Strike of 1926 was a nine-day strike in the United Kingdom from 3 to 12 May 1926, called by the Trades Union Congress in support of coal miners facing wage cuts and longer hours.</p></div></li></ol></section>
